---
description: Performance and efficiency rules for services and applications
version: 1.5.0
globs: [
  "perf/**",
  "performance/**",
  "benchmarks/**",
  "load/**",
  "stress/**",
  "**/*benchmark*",
  "**/*perf*",
  "**/*loadtest*",
  "**/*k6*",
  "apps/**/perf/**",
  "packages/**/perf/**",
  "**/*.py",
  "**/*.go",
  "**/*.rb",
  "**/*.java",
  "**/*.kt"
]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Establish performance budgets for latency, throughput, and resource use; measure against them in CI or canary.
- Include client-side RUM budgets for key journeys (e.g., LCP/CLS/TTFB/FID) and enforce via CI/canary.
- Profile hotspots with appropriate tools; optimize based on evidence, not guesswork.
- Prefer streaming/iterators over loading whole payloads into memory; avoid unnecessary copies.
- Batch external calls when possible; cache safely with clear TTLs and invalidation rules.
- Use timeouts and backpressure to protect services under load; validate concurrency safety.
- Keep indexes and query plans healthy; avoid unbounded scans and N+1 patterns.
- Track regressions with benchmarks or perf tests; gate releases on significant degradation.
